#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134097 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c67da0d8-518b-5fdb-b6ba-6c1c95c22d9b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Green's Theorem to Regions With Holes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "074f2b27-d82e-5431-893f-5cb420b7db07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130739} {:answer/id #uuid "4fb000df-3f30-5d92-833d-b570ce4d2fc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130740} {:answer/id #uuid "67a5cc30-ac62-56fb-b984-6bf8c55a68e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130741} {:answer/id #uuid "6d1f5867-3adf-5ebd-8085-208cd0303ff9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130742} {:answer/id #uuid "6da1aafe-3858-50f0-8369-80cd33a8831e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "074f2b27-d82e-5431-893f-5cb420b7db07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130739} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d6f2a4f-8215-5cfe-aa3b-409cfed8d343" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130738}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5d511ff2-5d88-51e6-9da4-d8015a261af1" :question/math-academy-id "q-126515" :question/problem "![](images/32/320a45751b2e718c66bb721cfcd78a2d206f08a9998fbbffddb1581ee995cf34.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}x\\,dy-y\\,dx,$ where $D$ is the region shown above." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-1,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}x\\,dy-y\\,dx & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(1-(-1))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =2{∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =2\\cdot ({4}^{2}-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (16-4) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498590 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133899 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56caab23-f54d-58ee-99db-99c651f78e5c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Circulation of a Vector Field Over a Region Containing Holes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a658638-403e-5ab9-a8f1-33237b22ab86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497887} {:answer/id #uuid "4d5743a8-8fd6-5394-b293-eb9fd93fef49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497979} {:answer/id #uuid "8e9eb833-f8ff-5a68-9ca4-2b64e1730afb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498127} {:answer/id #uuid "9d75ef58-226e-55fd-b151-11b12d2230bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498153} {:answer/id #uuid "f496543e-10b7-5658-8197-b5afed861eb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498334}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a658638-403e-5ab9-a8f1-33237b22ab86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497887} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7d01b58-0857-54fb-bdf6-61d33e711eeb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498438}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e2260d96-b984-5295-801c-28a9593008a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-126851" :question/problem "![](images/e9/e9892ef4efa3481ad02f7b8e38f1bae1876b196627204521d011656010297281.png)\n\nSuppose that $F$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ defined over the region $D$ above. Given that \n\n$$\n{∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=16,\\,{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=6,\\,{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=4,\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{1}$ is oriented counterclockwise and ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are oriented clockwise, calculate the value of ${∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the total circulation of a vector field over the boundary of a region containing holes, we add together the circulations over each *positively oriented* boundary.\n\nRemember that:\n\n- the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve ${C}_{1}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/b2/b20b2b911c2a417c26fa951d9b28efa296c265df25e9d06b635ef4846267b93b.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =16+6+4 \\\\  & =26.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369434 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c67da0d8-518b-5fdb-b6ba-6c1c95c22d9b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Green's Theorem to Regions With Holes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fe866fa-6339-5f10-8ce3-3d5938c3785e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369436} {:answer/id #uuid "0aafa5fa-6806-5c1a-bd6e-a8f0ec680d0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369437} {:answer/id #uuid "b169f03c-00d2-5df3-887b-9ea86b4a1f34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369438} {:answer/id #uuid "2e03cd88-a4dd-5d49-b397-096aeb5b4219" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369439} {:answer/id #uuid "8e91bdb9-02ae-5c29-aa67-a875b2bc2112" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e03cd88-a4dd-5d49-b397-096aeb5b4219" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369439} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2ee2d3e-bbe0-5737-8885-1738f355a09b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "32a18b85-d978-5b18-8fff-914bdccf82dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-126853" :question/problem "![](images/39/393bed476f2e8d84fc7e5dc721d77749f7f259834e03a94a48a08533ae9befa6.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}2y\\,dx+4x\\,dy,$ where $D$ is the region shown above." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=2y$ and $Q(x,y)=4x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}2y\\,dx+4x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(4-2)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =2{∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (6\\cdot 4-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (24-4) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 20 \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369462 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133899 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56caab23-f54d-58ee-99db-99c651f78e5c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Circulation of a Vector Field Over a Region Containing Holes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d7cf9a0-e8a9-528c-9faf-b2259025de3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369464} {:answer/id #uuid "ce1af42a-4bf9-5730-a278-44c2bcb271c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369465} {:answer/id #uuid "26f52db4-19ad-52bc-bdea-a43ddccabe76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369466} {:answer/id #uuid "74b55cd4-e132-5c25-af68-783e5644f0be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369467} {:answer/id #uuid "5901a191-1792-51d7-92cf-8ae7fe658d89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369468}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5901a191-1792-51d7-92cf-8ae7fe658d89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369468} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0c368b0-4e71-50a8-b81a-cf6d68ab083b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369463}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ca63e980-b1ab-5e66-b1ce-ccb3144f7558" :question/math-academy-id "q-126862" :question/problem "![](images/49/49b14da54c952d0585f7aa894d618838ddc91beb65216e0c18c014ba5ad268d7.png)\n\nSuppose that $F$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ defined over the region $D$ above. Given that \n\n$$\n{∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=9,\\,{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=-4,\\,{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=-6,\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{1}$ is oriented counterclockwise and ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are oriented clockwise, calculate the value of ${∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the total circulation of a vector field over the boundary of a region containing holes, we add together the circulations over each *positively oriented* boundary.\n\nRemember that:\n\n- the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve ${C}_{1}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/a8/a8e93055fb9a460ab7757475c9c381c191204eae72231921da870b8d727bf988.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =9+(-4)+(-6) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498490 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133886 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c67da0d8-518b-5fdb-b6ba-6c1c95c22d9b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Green's Theorem to Regions With Holes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb8d995d-0d7c-54d6-8c3f-aa2cc0e562a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498216} {:answer/id #uuid "ce93c3a1-776f-5631-aafd-89bd7f33c5b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498268} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe50e10-ec80-526e-8c44-4ebed28fb715" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498270} {:answer/id #uuid "e1f112d4-518e-59d2-a8ae-9b7896ed80c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498304} {:answer/id #uuid "e6e01110-89b2-522a-b30e-7b877b8b16ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfe50e10-ec80-526e-8c44-4ebed28fb715" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498270} :answer-field/id #uuid "30362ef7-7428-53da-a7f2-7fe7cc3d3d5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "09c35a82-4469-5857-aed4-331c374b8ab3" :question/math-academy-id "q-126895" :question/problem "![](images/0d/0db447407835f74476edd20ed5327ff3cc570905f744bbc6c29a66926913ecb5.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}(1-4y)\\,dx+(2+5x)\\,dy,$ where $D$ is the annular region shown above." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=1-4y$ and $Q(x,y)=2+5x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-4,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}dx+x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5-(-4))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}9\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =9\\,\\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =9\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}-\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}) \\\\  & =9\\cdot 5\\pi  \\\\  & =45\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
